{#
  The site's form challenge, drawn inside a public form ahead of its submit
  button: `widget(contactForm.challenge, "contact", "message")`.

  It is only ever handed a challenge for a stranger, and only while one is on,
  so a form that calls it with nothing draws nothing. The default theme knows
  how to draw hCaptcha: an empty `div.h-captcha` with the site key, which
  `static/hcaptcha.js` fills once the page has loaded. The shell loads that
  script whenever a drawn form carries the challenge, so a form that draws
  this needs no script of its own.

  The widget is an iframe hCaptcha draws, reached with Tab like any field. The
  group around it is labelled, and says what happens when it never appears:
  the form still sends, and what it sends waits for somebody to look at it.
#}
{% macro widget(challenge, prefix, noun) %}
{% if challenge and challenge.provider == "hcaptcha" %}
<div class="form-challenge" role="group" aria-labelledby="{{ prefix }}-challenge-label" aria-describedby="{{ prefix }}-challenge-hint">
  <span class="form-challenge-label" id="{{ prefix }}-challenge-label">Spam check</span>
  <div class="h-captcha" data-sitekey="{{ challenge.siteKey }}"></div>
  <span class="{{ prefix }}-hint" id="{{ prefix }}-challenge-hint">Run by hCaptcha. If it does not appear, or JavaScript is off, your {{ noun }} is still sent but may need a manual check.</span>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
